.TH KLAMAV-PY 1 "2026-09-30" "KlamAV-Py 0.1.13" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
klamav-py \- command-line virus scanning through the ClamAV daemon
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B klamav-py
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-tcp
.IR host [: port ]]
.B scan
.I path
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B klamav-py
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-tcp
.IR host [: port ]]
.B ping
.br
.B klamav-py
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-tcp
.IR host [: port ]]
.RB [ \-\-acknowledge
.IR path ]...
.RB [ \-\-unacknowledge
.IR value ]...
.RB [ \-\-list\-acknowledged ]
.br
.B klamav-py \-\-version
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B klamav-py
scans files and directories by delegating the analysis to
.BR clamd (8)
through its native protocol, without invoking a shell or external programs.
Files are sent to clamd as a stream
.RB ( INSTREAM ),
so the daemon does not need read permission on the user's paths.
By default, files share a persistent session
.RB ( IDSESSION ).
.PP
The command does not depend on Qt and runs with the system Python alone,
for use from scripts and by the scheduled scan.
The graphical interface is provided by
.BR klamav-py-gui (1).
.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI scan " path"
Scan a file or, recursively, a directory.
Only one path is accepted per invocation.
.TP
.B ping
Check that clamd responds.
.
.SH OPTIONS
Global options must come before the command.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Path to the clamd Unix socket.
Default:
.IR /run/clamav/clamd.ctl .
.TP
.BI \-\-tcp " host\fR[\fP:port\fR]\fP"
Connect to clamd via TCP instead of a Unix socket
(default port 3310).
For IPv6, use the form
.IR [address]:port .
Incompatible with
.BR \-\-socket .
See
.B SECURITY
before using it.
.SS Acknowledgement options
They record that a reported detection has been checked, so that later
scans stop counting it (see
.BR "Detections that are not quarantined" ).
They are used without a command; with more than one, they run in the
order below.
.TP
.BI \-\-acknowledge " path"
Rescan
.I path
through clamd and record the acknowledgement only if it is infected with
a detection that is reported but not moved (heuristic signature or mail
archive).
A clean file, a detection that would be quarantined, a symbolic link, or
a file that changes during the check are refused without recording
anything.
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-unacknowledge " value"
Revoke an acknowledgement:
.I value
is the path of the file (its current content is hashed) or the hash
prefix printed by
.BR \-\-list\-acknowledged ,
for files that no longer exist.
An ambiguous or unknown prefix is an error and nothing is revoked.
Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-acknowledged
List the acknowledgements: hash prefix, signature, first path seen,
date of the acknowledgement and of the last scan that found it.
.SS Scan options
.TP
.BI \-\-quarantine " directory"
Move infected files to
.IR directory ,
which is created with permissions 0700 if missing; an existing directory
with wider permissions is restricted to 0700, with a warning.
A relative path is resolved against the current directory.
The directory is always excluded from the scan, so files already isolated
are not detected again: for this reason it cannot contain the
.I path
being scanned, which would be excluded entirely.
Volatile directories produce a warning or an error, and some detections
are only reported (see
.BR SECURITY ).
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " directory"
Exclude
.I directory
from traversal: its contents are not even read.
Can be repeated.
It is an error (exit status 2) if
.I directory
is not a directory, since single files would be scanned anyway, or if it
contains
.IR path ,
which would be excluded entirely.
A directory that does not exist yet, or that lies outside
.IR path ,
only produces a warning.
.TP
.BI \-\-report\-only " directory"
With
.BR \-\-quarantine ,
infected files under
.I directory
are reported but not moved.
Can be repeated; adds to the mail archives already protected.
.TP
.B \-\-quarantine\-all
With
.BR \-\-quarantine ,
also move heuristic detections and files in mail archives, which by
default are only reported.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-stream\-size " bytes"
Files larger than
.I bytes
are not sent to clamd and are reported as unverified, without being
counted as errors.
Default: 25 MB, matching
.B StreamMaxLength
in
.BR clamd.conf (5).
A value of 0 disables the check.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Do not show clean files, individual unverified files, or skipped entries.
Infections, errors, and the summary are still shown.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persistent
Open a new connection to clamd for every file instead of using a
persistent session.
Slower: only useful to isolate session-related problems.
.TP
.BI \-\-session\-batch\-size " n"
Number of files after which the persistent session is closed and
reopened.
Default: 500.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-errors " file"
Write one line per error to
.IR file ,
with the path and the reason separated by a tab.
The file is created with permissions 0600, without following symbolic
links, and pre-existing files owned by other users are refused.
.
.SH OUTPUT
One line per file:
.BR OK: ,
.BR INFETTO:
(with the signature and the quarantine outcome, if any),
.B NON VERIFICATO
for files over the size limit, or
.B ERRORE
on standard error.
An acknowledged detection prints
.B GIÀ VALUTATO
at every scan, also with
.BR \-\-quiet ,
and is not counted among the infected files.
A subdirectory that cannot be read is reported once on standard error
with
.B CARTELLA NON LEGGIBILE
(and in the
.B \-\-log\-errors
file); its contents are not checked.
It is counted separately, not among the errors: if it is expected (a
directory created with sudo, a container bind mount), exclude it with
.BR \-\-exclude .
The messages are in Italian.
A summary with the totals follows and, if there were errors, a count
per error type.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No infections found, even if some files or subdirectories could not be
read or verified.
.TP
.B 1
Infections found, even if quarantining some of them failed.
.TP
.B 2
Fatal error: the path to scan does not exist, is a broken symbolic link,
is neither a directory nor a regular file (a FIFO, a device such as
.IR /dev/null ),
or is a directory that cannot be read, each with its own message;
unusable quarantine directory, clamd
unreachable or protocol error,
.B \-\-log\-errors
file cannot be opened, invalid command line.
A communication error after the scan has started takes precedence over
infections already found.
.PP
For
.BR ping :
0 if clamd responds, 2 otherwise.
.PP
For the acknowledgement options: 0 if every value was handled, 2 if at
least one was refused (that one leaves the register unchanged).
.PP
In the scheduled scan, codes 1 and 2 trigger the desktop notification
through
.BR klamav-scan-notify.service .
Unreadable subdirectories leave the code at 0, so they show up only in
the journal.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INVOCATION_ID
Set by systemd for each service.
If present, a volatile quarantine directory passed with
.B \-\-quarantine
becomes an error instead of a warning (see
.BR SECURITY ).
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I \%/usr/lib/systemd/user/klamav-scan.service
.TQ
.I \%/usr/lib/systemd/user/klamav-scan.timer
User units for the scheduled home directory scan, run in a sandbox at
the lowest CPU and I/O priority.
The quarantine directory used by the timer is changed from the Settings
of
.BR klamav-py-gui (1).
.TP
.I \%/usr/lib/systemd/user/klamav-scan-notify.service
Desktop notification, started only by the scan's
.BR OnFailure= .
.TP
.I \%~/.local/share/klamav-py/quarantine
Quarantine directory of the scheduled scan (0700).
It holds the isolated files (0400) and the service files (0600):
the index
.IR index.json ,
the lock file
.IR index.json.lock ,
which is never truncated or rewritten, and the temporary files of atomic
writes.
An unreadable index is renamed to
.I index.json.corrupt-*
and never deleted, so that it can be recovered by hand.
Each quarantine in progress is recorded in a hidden file
.I .<name>.intent
(and
.I .<name>.copy
if the file is copied from another file system): if the operation is
interrupted, for example by a crash, the next start of the CLI or the
GUI completes it or rolls it back, leaving the original file in place in
that case.
.TP
.I \%~/.local/share/klamav-py/acknowledged.json
Register of acknowledged detections (0600), written atomically, with the
lock file
.IR acknowledged.json.lock .
An invalid register is renamed to
.I acknowledged.json.corrupt-*
and never deleted.
Entries not found by any scan for 90 days are removed.
.
.SH SECURITY
.SS Quarantine directory
The quarantine cannot reside in volatile directories:
.IR /tmp ,
.IR /var/tmp ,
.I /run
and
.I /dev
are rejected, as are paths that the unit's sandbox directives make private
or inaccessible.
The check is performed on the already expanded and resolved path, so it
also applies to symbolic links such as
.IR /var/run .
.PP
Reason: the scanning unit uses
.BR PrivateTmp=true .
A quarantine in
.I /var/tmp
would end up in the service's private temporary directory, which systemd
deletes, together with the index, when the scan ends: infected files would
be destroyed without any error or notification.
.PP
Directories on other
.BR tmpfs " or " ramfs
file systems are accepted with a warning, because their contents are lost
on reboot.
.PP
With
.B \-\-quarantine
on the command line, in the foreground, a volatile directory only
produces a warning: there,
.I /tmp
is the real, visible one.
Under systemd (with
.B INVOCATION_ID
set) it is an error instead, with exit status 2.
.
.SS Detections that are not quarantined
With
.BR \-\-quarantine ,
heuristic detections
.RB ( Heuristics.* )
and files in KMail/Akonadi, Thunderbird, Evolution, and Maildir mail
archives are reported but not moved, to avoid damaging the user's
mailboxes.
Without
.B \-\-quarantine
they are reported like the others.
.B \-\-report\-only
extends this rule to other directories,
.B \-\-quarantine\-all
disables it.
.PP
After checking one, delete it or record the acknowledgement with
.BR \-\-acknowledge :
later scans print
.B GIÀ VALUTATO
for it and no longer count it as infected, so the exit status and the
scheduled scan notification are no longer triggered by a detection
already checked.
The key is the SHA-256 of the content plus the signature, not the path:
a message that moves from
.I new/
to
.I cur/
in a maildir stays acknowledged, while a changed content is reported
again.
The register is consulted only for detections that would not be moved
anyway: an acknowledgement never hides one that would be quarantined.
A new detection keeps exit status 1.
.SS TCP connection
clamd does not support TLS: with
.B \-\-tcp
the contents of scanned files travel in clear text.
Use it only with localhost or trusted networks, or through an
.BR ssh (1)
or
.BR stunnel (8)
tunnel.
There is no automatic fallback between Unix socket and TCP.
.PP
Enabling
.B TCPSocket
in
.BR clamd.conf (5)
is discouraged: unlike the Unix socket, which is protected by its
permissions, a TCP port lets any local user use
clamd as a scanning oracle.
.PP
The scheduled system scan uses the connection set in
.BR klamav-py-gui (1).
With TCP its drop-in allows network access by overriding
.B PrivateNetwork=no
and
.B RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_UNIX AF_INET AF_INET6
while keeping the filter; with the Unix socket the unit has no network
access.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
Scan the home directory with quarantine, showing only problems:
.PP
.RS
.EX
klamav\-py scan ~ \-\-quarantine ~/.local/share/klamav\-py/quarantine \-\-quiet
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check that clamd responds on a non-standard socket:
.PP
.RS
.EX
klamav\-py \-\-socket /run/clamd.scan/clamd.sock ping
.EE
.RE
.PP
Acknowledge a phishing message left in the KMail trash after checking
it, list the acknowledgements, and revoke one by hash prefix:
.PP
.RS
.EX
journalctl \-\-user \-u klamav\-scan.service | grep INFETTO
klamav\-py \-\-acknowledge ~/.local/share/local\-mail/trash/new/1695\&.R42.host
klamav\-py \-\-list\-acknowledged
klamav\-py \-\-unacknowledge 3f2a9c01be47
.EE
.RE
.
